WebGPU: readTexture in the browser completes from the browser's event loop

With a device from PlatformData::context in the browser, readTexture mapped its read-back buffer and then waited
for the map in a loop calling wgpuInstanceProcessEvents. The map's callback (AllowProcessEvents) is filed under
the instance the device was imported into, never bgfx's own, and the browser resolves a map only from its event
loop, which the waiting loop never returns to: the page hangs on the first read. With such a device the map now
uses the spontaneous callback mode the timer and occlusion query read-backs use: readTexture returns at once, and
the callback copies the texels and frees the read when the browser resolves the map, between the frames before
the read is due. readBuffer and requestScreenShot wait the same way and are not changed here.

diff --git a/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp b/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
--- a/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
@@ -1981,7 +1981,14 @@ WGPU_IMPORT
 
 			wgpuRelease(readTexture.buffer);
 
-			*(bool*)(_userdata2) = true;
+			if (NULL == _userdata2)
+			{
+				bx::deleteObject(g_allocator, &readTexture);
+			}
+			else
+			{
+				*(bool*)(_userdata2) = true;
+			}
 		}
 
 		struct ReadBuffer
@@ -2145,6 +2152,26 @@ WGPU_IMPORT
 				.texelSize     = blockInfo.blockSize,
 			};
 
+			if (WGPUCallbackMode_AllowSpontaneous == m_callbackMode)
+			{
+				// In the browser this thread cannot wait for the map: the browser completes it from its event loop,
+				// between the frames that pass before the read is due. The callback owns the read.
+				WGPU_CHECK(wgpuBufferMapAsync(
+					  readTextureBuffer
+					, WGPUMapMode_Read
+					, 0
+					, copySize
+					, {
+						.nextInChain = NULL,
+						.mode        = m_callbackMode,
+						.callback    = readTextureCb,
+						.userdata1   = BX_NEW(g_allocator, ReadTexture)(readTexture),
+						.userdata2   = NULL,
+					}) );
+
+				return;
+			}
+
 			WGPU_CHECK(wgpuBufferMapAsync(
 				  readTextureBuffer
 				, WGPUMapMode_Read
